{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 10.241,
   "text": "Nobody listens to a tiny country radio station at three in the morning. At least, that's what I thought."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 10.841,
   "end": 15.172,
   "text": "The old night host left one sticky note on my microphone."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 15.672,
   "end": 21.475,
   "text": "If the request line lights up after three... don't answer. And never put the caller on the air."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 22.275,
   "end": 27.331,
   "text": "All winter, that line stayed dark. Just me, the snow, and sad old songs."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 28.031,
   "end": 32.809,
   "text": "Then, one night, at three-oh-six... the little red light started blinking."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 35.609,
   "end": 38.681,
   "text": "I let it ring. Through two whole songs."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 39.481,
   "end": 42.511,
   "text": "Then it stopped... and so did the music."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 43.911,
   "end": 48.839,
   "text": "I grabbed my headphones. And I heard my own voice. Live. On the air."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 49.739,
   "end": 53.749,
   "text": "We've got a caller on the line, folks. Go ahead... you're on."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 54.949,
   "end": 58.811,
   "text": "Something breathed into the line. Slow. Wet. Patient."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 59.811,
   "end": 64.461,
   "text": "Then it asked for a dedication... for the man alone in the studio."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 65.061,
   "end": 67.429,
   "text": "Tell him I'm on the stairs."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 70.029,
   "end": 74.595,
   "text": "I yanked every cable out of the board. Dead air. Total silence."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 75.995,
   "end": 81.691,
   "text": "Then the stairwell door creaked open behind me... and my own voice whispered... You're on."
  }
 ],
